---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Composition pipelines"
  description="Three strategies the engine uses to turn Nitro resources into screen pixels: NSCR BG, NCER OBJ, tad-driven widget table."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: '2D Art', href: `${base}/field-guide/2d-art/` },
    { label: 'Composition' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Strategy A: NSCR-driven BG screen</h2>
  <p>
    Inputs: <strong>NCGR</strong> tilebank (8×8 tiles) +
    <strong>NCLR</strong> palette + <strong>NSCR</strong> screen map.
    Output: 256×192 BG image (32×24 cells).
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`     ┌──────────┐
NCLR │ palette  │──────┐
     └──────────┘      │
     ┌──────────┐      ▼
NCGR │ tilebank │──┐  ┌────────────────────┐
     └──────────┘  └─►│ compose_nscr_screen│──► 256×192 RGBA
     ┌──────────┐  ┌─►│  for each cell:    │
NSCR │ screen   │──┘  │   tile_idx (10b)   │
     │ (32×24)  │     │   palette_bank(4b) │
     └──────────┘     │   hflip / vflip    │
                      └────────────────────┘`}</code></pre>
  <pre><code>{`# src/translator/_sprite_decode.py::compose_nscr_screen
for cell_y in range(24):
    for cell_x in range(32):
        word = nscr.cells[cell_y * 32 + cell_x]
        tile = word & 0x3FF
        hflip = (word >> 10) & 1
        vflip = (word >> 11) & 1
        bank  = (word >> 12) & 0xF
        tile_pixels = ncgr.tile(tile)              # 8×8 indices
        if hflip: tile_pixels = flip_x(tile_pixels)
        if vflip: tile_pixels = flip_y(tile_pixels)
        for py in range(8):
            for px in range(8):
                idx = tile_pixels[py][px]
                color = nclr.bank(bank)[idx]
                out[cell_y*8 + py][cell_x*8 + px] = color
`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Used by 1,099 NSCR-bearing containers. Examples:
    <code>buyitem.lzs</code> shop chrome, <code>title_pack.ofs</code> castle
    art, every map-screen overlay.
  </p>

  <h2>Strategy B: NCER-driven OBJ sprite</h2>
  <p>
    Inputs: <strong>NCGR</strong> tilebank +
    <strong>NCLR</strong> palette + <strong>NCER</strong> cell definition.
    Output: one or more sprite cells, each composed of multiple OAM "chips."
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`     ┌──────────┐
NCLR │ palette  │──────────┐
     └──────────┘          │
     ┌──────────┐          ▼
NCGR │ tilebank │──┐ ┌─────────────────────┐
     └──────────┘  └►│ compose_ncer_cell   │──► per-cell PNG
                    │   for each OBJ:     │
     ┌──────────┐   │     (x,y,w,h,tile,  │
NCER │ cells +  │──►│      palette,flip)  │
     │ OAM list │   │     blit into canvas│
     └──────────┘   └─────────────────────┘`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Each cell holds <code>obj_count</code> OAM entries; per OBJ the
    <code>(shape, size)</code> pair selects pixel dimensions via the
    standard NDS lookup:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>size →</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>shape 00 (square)</strong></td><td>8×8</td><td>16×16</td><td>32×32</td><td>64×64</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>shape 01 (wide)</strong></td><td>16×8</td><td>32×8</td><td>32×16</td><td>64×32</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>shape 10 (tall)</strong></td><td>8×16</td><td>8×32</td><td>16×32</td><td>32×64</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Used by 926 NCER-bearing containers.</p>

  <h2>Strategy C: <code>tad</code> widget table</h2>
  <p>
    Inputs: <strong>NCER</strong> cell (selected by <code>cell_id</code>) +
    <strong>NCLR</strong> + the <code>tad</code>/widget-table record
    <code>(palette, sub, flags, x, y)</code>.
    Output: composed UI screen at the abs_x/abs_y of each record.
  </p>
  <p>
    The table can sit in two places:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A <code>tad</code> RESO entry inside the asset container (e.g.
      <code>buyitem.lzs</code>'s <code>tad</code> entry).</li>
    <li>Inside an overlay's <code>.rodata</code> (e.g. ov070's table at
      <code>0x0215A538</code> for the buyitem screen).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Either way the engine walks the table, calls a sprite-constructor for
    each entry, and the constructor resolves the asset bytes from the
    content cache. See
    <a href={`${base}/field-guide/how-the-game-works/sprite-pipeline/`}>sprite pipeline</a>
    for the runtime side.
  </p>
  <p>
    50 containers ship with a static recipe: 37 with a <code>rnan</code>-only
    table, 8 with <code>tad</code>, 5 with <code>nib</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Strategy D: code-driven (no static recipe)</h2>
  <p>
    123 NCER-bearing containers ship without any static placement table.
    The composition logic is hard-coded in the controller/body overlay
    pair. Examples:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>FUN_02174604</code>: <code>place(slot, x=20, y=0, w=216, h=64, type=2)</code></li>
    <li><code>FUN_02174760</code>: <code>place(slot, x=13, y=40, w=230, h=112, type=2)</code></li>
    <li><code>FUN_021747A8</code>: <code>place(slot, x=13, y=60, w=230, h=94, type=2)</code></li>
    <li><code>FUN_02177FE4</code>: two placements at <code>(8,64)</code> and <code>(8,120)</code>, w=240 h=28</li>
    <li><code>FUN_0217B9D8</code>: <code>place(slot, x=13, y=60, w=230, h=94, type=2)</code></li>
    <li><code>FUN_02181D24</code>: looks up <code>(x, y)</code> from a 6-entry table at <code>0x0218CBE6</code></li>
    <li><code>FUN_02174B80</code>: triple-nested loop, 144 sprites in a 3×4×12 grid (buyitem catalog)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Runtime shadow-OAM</h2>
  <p>
    The engine never writes OAM RAM (<code>0x07000000</code> / <code>0x07000400</code>)
    directly during scene composition. It builds a <strong>shadow OAM</strong>
    in main RAM via <code>STR</code>/<code>STRH</code> at sprite-slot addresses
    computed from <code>*0x021907BC + i*0x40 + field_offset</code> chains.
    At VBlank, <code>FUN_02185BF8</code> (ov137) and <code>FUN_0207001C</code>
    (arm9) DMA the shadow buffer into hardware OAM.
  </p>
  <p>OAM/VRAM transfer wrappers (all four resolve to <code>FUN_02017D9C</code> = DMA0):</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Address</th><th>Role</th><th>Destination</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x020769C0</code></td><td>OAM main</td><td><code>0x07000000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A00</code></td><td>OAM sub</td><td><code>0x07000400 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A40</code></td><td>OBJ VRAM main</td><td><code>0x06400000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A7C</code></td><td>OBJ VRAM sub</td><td><code>0x06600000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>src/translator/_sprite_decode.py</code> — <code>compose_nscr_screen</code>, <code>compose_ncer_cell</code>, <code>OBJ_SIZE_LUT</code></li>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/DISCOVERIES.md</code> — verified placement recipes</li>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/BUYITEM_RECIPE_CRACKED.md</code> — Strategy C worked example</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
